 `Anchor` accepts heading `depth`, `index`, and `description` metadata plus an `activationOffset`.
 Its current link stays synchronized on click and scroll, including at the end of the document.
+A heading becomes current once its top reaches the native fragment landing line, the root
+`scroll-padding-top` plus the heading's `scroll-margin-top`, or the numeric `activationOffset` in CSS
+pixels, whichever is lower on screen, within one CSS pixel. The landing line follows text scaling, so
+fragment links keep the marker on their destination with enlarged root text. Percentage scroll padding
+resolves against the scrolling element's height; `auto` and unresolved values count as zero.
 `ScrollProgress` derives reading progress from the document and pins the indicator to the top or
 bottom viewport edge. Both use the single root `UIPrimitives` runtime.
 
+Pass `targetId` to `ScrollProgress` to measure one content element instead. Progress starts when
+the element reaches the root scroll-padding landing line and finishes when its bottom enters the
+viewport. Targets shorter than that reading area finish once fully visible; empty targets remain
+at zero. Values stay between zero and 100 while scrolling beyond the target. An omitted or missing
+target retains document progress. The runtime recalculates on scroll, resize, and content reflow,
+and reconnects its resize observer after page navigation. No second controller is needed.
+
